// ===========================================================================
//  walk.hml — THE PLAYABLE WALKAROUND.                      W3-0b.
// ===========================================================================
//
//  The first time anyone MOVES through this world instead of looking at a
//  screenshot of it. Mouse-look + WASD, a fly toggle, a live time-of-day
//  scrub, a weather cycle, teleports to every shot.hml scene, and an on-screen
//  budget readout so the cost of what you are looking at is visible while you
//  look at it.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  IT RENDERS THROUGH THE REAL FRAME GRAPH. THERE IS NO SECOND ONE.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  `src/render/world_render.hml` (W3-0a) owns stages 8..23 and 25..28 of
//  ARCHITECTURE.md §4. This file NEVER defines the frame graph function —
//  `ci_imports.sh` R7 exists precisely to stop a harness carrying a private
//  copy, and W3-0's acceptance greps every tool for a local definition of it
//  and requires zero hits. (Which is why that grep's pattern is not written out
//  literally anywhere in this file: the comment would be the hit.) What it owns
//  is
//  the caller's half of the frame, which the import wall leaves with the
//  caller because `src/render/**` may not import `src/art/**`:
//
//      stage 6   tod_eval  -> the frame graph's RenderEnv
//      stage 7   skygen's rolling re-bake
//      stage 24  the HUD (here: the budget readout)
//
//  plus the world itself, which the frame graph WALKS but never BUILDS.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  WHY THIS FILE HAS ITS OWN WORLD BUILDER, AND WHAT THAT COSTS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  `tools/shot.hml` ends in `main();`, so it cannot be imported, and W3-0b owns
//  `tools/walk.hml` and nothing else — editing shot.hml to extract a shared
//  builder is another agent's file (CLAUDE.md §3). So the ground material rules
//  (`ground_cell` / `ground_vcol` / the path), the apron fan and the structure
//  panel helpers are RE-DERIVED here rather than shared. This is real
//  duplication and it is reported as such; the fix is W3-1 `worldgen.hml` +
//  W3-2 `chunk.hml` + `src/render/terrain_render.hml`, which is where all of it
//  belongs. Until then, the ONE thing that is shared and must stay shared is
//  the height field: `terrain_h` comes from `world_render.hml`, so the ground
//  the player stands on is the same ground the frame graph lays its light pools
//  on, to the last bit.
//
//  What is DELIBERATELY different from shot.hml, because a walkaround is not a
//  screenshot:
//    * the world is WORLD-ANCHORED, not camera-anchored. shot scatters props in
//      a seeded stream around a fixed camera; that world would slide with you.
//      Here every prop and every material is a pure function of its own
//      position, so walking 200 m and walking back shows you the same trees.
//    * terrain chunks STREAM. A ring is meshed around the player, cached, and
//      re-baked on a rolling cursor, which is what `g_BUDGET_CHUNKGEN_MS` in
//      core/config.hml is for.
//    * there are SITES — towers, camps and ruins on a 96 m lattice — because
//      "is there anything on the horizon worth walking toward" is one of the
//      questions this build exists to answer, and you cannot answer it with an
//      empty heath.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  RUNNING IT
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//      hemlockc -O1 tools/walk.hml -o /tmp/walk
//      DISPLAY=:0 /tmp/walk                      # interactive, x3 upscale
//      DISPLAY=:0 /tmp/walk --demo 20 --shots /tmp/walkshots
//      SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/walk --selftest        # CI smoke test
//
//  Headless it degrades and does not die: SDL_SetRelativeMouseMode ALWAYS
//  returns -1 under the dummy driver and the WARP hint does not rescue it
//  (CLAUDE.md §5). The status is reported, mouse-look is disabled, and the
//  walk runs on the keyboard path exactly as it would with a mouse.
// ===========================================================================

